id: pm-brief-00tc
title: Adopt pm CLI 2026.8.30 and stop pinning which way the SDK handles an incomplete merge receipt
description: "Dependabot cannot green a host CLI bump here because a packaging test asserts the devDependency equals a constant declared in test/version-contract.ts, and dependabot never edits test files. Moving both together adopts 2026.8.30, which also carries the fix for the npm 12 package install breakage. Bumping surfaced a second problem: listMergeReceipts has changed its handling of structurally incomplete receipts three times, throwing, then defaulting the missing fields and returning the receipt, and now dropping it entirely, so a guard that pinned the SDK's choice failed on a routine version bump with no behaviour of ours changing. The guard now pins the invariant that survives all three, that no incomplete receipt may yield a usable decision, and asserts the fixture exists on disk so an empty result cannot satisfy it vacuously. Reported upstream as pm-cli issue 1161."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-08-30T17:20:52.762Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-31T11:41:04.250Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-30T17:20:54.993Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-30T17:20:54.993Z"
author: claude
resolution: "Adopted pm CLI 2026.8.30 by moving the devDependency pin and the version-contract constant in test/version-contract.ts in one commit, which is the only shape Dependabot cannot produce, and replaced the merge-receipt guard's version-specific expectation with the invariant that survives all three SDK behaviours."
expected_result: "Bumping the pinned host CLI changes only which binary the gates run, leaving the tracked-item health verdict and the merge-receipt guard unaffected."
actual_result: "The bump also broke a guard that had pinned one of the SDK's three historical handlings of a structurally incomplete merge receipt. listMergeReceipts threw up to 2026.8.12, then defaulted the missing fields and returned the receipt through 2026.8.24, and now drops it and returns an empty array, so the guard failed on a routine version bump with none of our behaviour changing. Tracked health showed no drift under the newly pinned binary, and the suite passed 353 of 353 once the guard was rewritten to assert that no incomplete receipt yields a usable decision, with a fixture-existence check so an empty result cannot satisfy it vacuously."
close_reason: "Host CLI and its version-contract constant moved together to 2026.8.30 with no history drift under the pinned binary, and the merge-receipt guard now pins the version-independent invariant with a fixture-existence assertion proving non-vacuity. Suite passes 353 of 353."
body: ""
